  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-narra-channel",
      "text": "[](https://github.com/NetMind-AI/dsh-narra-channel/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n\nEnglish | [简体中文](README.zh.md)\n\n`dsh-narra-channel` is an independent, third-party DeepSeek Harness Profile Bundle that connects a Harness Agent Preset to Narra Messenger. It does not modify DeepSeek Harness or the Narra frontend/backend.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> DeepSeek Harness is in developer preview. This plugin version targets Harness `0.1.0-rc.8` and may need an update for other release trains."
    },
    {
      "section": "Scope",
      "text": "This repository contains only the Narra channel plugin: its Harness integration, settings UI, Gateway protocol implementation, tests, and plugin documentation. Installing, containerizing, or operating DeepSeek Harness and Narra services is outside the plugin's scope."
    },
    {
      "section": "Capabilities",
      "text": "- Select an Agent Preset in Harness Settings → Narra and paste the complete binding instruction supplied by Narra.\n- Extract only the setup-guide URL; the plugin never executes scripts or commands from the guide.\n- Submit a contact-facing name and bio derived from the selected preset, with an optional identity editor before binding.\n- Store binding URLs and Gateway bearer tokens in Harness Credentials instead of ordinary settings or logs.\n- Run one independent Channel Worker per binding. Messages are serialized within a binding while different bindings can work concurrently.\n- Map each Narra room to a deterministic, recoverable Harness Session and avoid rerunning completed duplicate invocations.\n- Stream text replies through the Narra Gateway.\n- Recognize `voice_instructions` and use short, fast, speech-friendly replies for that turn."
    },
    {
      "section": "Capabilities",
      "text": "Voice mode transports transcribed text and streamed response text. This plugin does not transmit raw audio."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- Node.js `^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0`\n- pnpm `11.7.0`\n- DeepSeek Harness `0.1.0-rc.8`\n- A configured model provider in Harness\n- A fresh Narra agent binding instruction"
    },
    {
      "section": "Build and install from source",
      "text": "The npm package has not been published yet. Build a tarball from a trusted checkout:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/NetMind-AI/dsh-narra-channel.git\ncd dsh-narra-channel\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile\npnpm typecheck\n\nRestart the `web` profile, then open Harness Settings → Narra:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Build and install from source",
      "text": "1. Select an Agent Preset.\n2. Paste the full binding instruction or its setup-guide URL.\n3. Review the proposed Narra identity and edit it if needed.\n4. Select **Bind and start listening** and wait for the status to become `connected`.\n\nRepeat the process to create additional Narra agents. Removing a binding stops its worker and deletes its Harness credential; version `0.1.5` does not remotely delete the agent from Narra."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security and data handling",
      "text": "- The setup guide parser accepts only the binding status, guide revision, Gateway URL, and Gateway token fields required by the protocol.\n- The plugin calls the fixed profile-report, guide-acknowledgement, and Gateway endpoints derived from the supplied setup-guide URL.\n- Gateway credentials are never intentionally exposed to the model.\n- Narra message text, sender/room metadata, recent context, and streamed agent replies cross the Narra Gateway as part of normal operation.\n- Harness Credentials reduce accidental secret exposure through ordinary settings and API responses, but they are not an operating-system isolation boundary. Host and process isolation remain the Harness operator's responsibility and are outside this plugin's scope.\n- Third-party Harness plugins run in the Harness process. Review source and install only versions you trust."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security and data handling",
      "text": "Please report vulnerabilities according to [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Current limitations",
      "text": "- A binding processes only one message at a time. Multiple rooms for the same agent may queue behind a long task.\n- Attachments are preserved only as source metadata; version `0.1.5` does not download or return files.\n- The plugin uses recent context supplied by the Gateway and does not expose the Gateway token to model tools for separate history retrieval.\n- Runtime update-guide instructions are not executed automatically. Upgrade the package and restart the profile explicitly.\n- Harness is a developer preview. Compatibility is currently pinned to `0.1.0-rc.8` rather than promised across preview releases."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile\npnpm typecheck\npnpm test\npnpm build"
    },
    {
